diff --git a/docs/transform-progress.md b/docs/transform-progress.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..10a245e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/transform-progress.md
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+# Transform progress reporting
+
+`sqlite-utils transform DATABASE TABLE --progress` reports copied-row counts on
+standard error. The library accepts `Table.transform(progress=callback)`, where
+the callback receives `(copied_rows, total_rows)` before copying and after each
+successful batch. The total is counted inside the transformation transaction.
+Callback exceptions follow the ordinary rollback path. A final copied-row update
+means row copying finished; index recreation and transaction commit still have to
+succeed before the transformation itself is complete. `--progress --sql` is a
+usage error, and `transform_sql()` remains unchanged.
+
+The progress path uses batches of 10,000 rows. It prefers a non-partial unique
+index whose key columns are all `NOT NULL`, ascending, and `BINARY` collated.
+Otherwise it uses an accessible hidden rowid on an ordinary rowid table. If the
+table has neither safe key, it uses the existing single copy operation and
+reports coarse start and finish counts. Batching does not promise lower peak
+storage use: the source and replacement tables coexist until the transaction
+commits.
